gapAnalysis.detail:
The Core project contains zero Entity, Aggregate, or Value Object classes. FileService, DiscussionService, ReviewService, and every other service operate directly on *Response DTOs (FileResponse, DiscussionResponse) which are output models, not domain models. Business invariants ('user must have permission', 'rating must be 0 when disabled') are enforced as raw if-blocks in application service methods rather than as methods on an aggregate. Every service is a transaction script.

Before (DiscussionService):
  if (permissionCheckTask.Result)
      return discussionTask.Result;
  else
      throw new SeismicForbiddenFileException(...);

After:
  public class DiscussionThread {
    public void AssertViewerHasAccess(bool hasPermission) {
      if (!hasPermission) throw new SeismicForbiddenFileException(...);
    }
  }

ContentDetailService.GetContentDetailAsync coordinates 7 concurrent provider calls, applies conditional rating masking (a business rule), merges file extra info via FileHelper, and conditionally fetches PageStorage based on file format. This is domain policy expressed as infrastructure plumbing. The 'rating=0 when disabled' and 'navigation flag' rules belong on the File aggregate.

Before:
  if (!doccenterSettingResponse.EnableRating.Value)
      extraFileResponse.Rating = 0;
  _fileHelper.MergeExtendInfo(contentDetailResponse.File, extraFileResponse, showNavigation, fileVariants);

After:
  file.ApplyTenantSettings(doccenterSetting); // domain method on FileEntity

FolderService creates a ChildrenAllReFillerManager via 'new' inside its constructor, passing through all injected dependencies manually. This is a layer violation: the application service acts as a factory for a concrete infrastructure class, and the dependency cannot be mocked in unit tests.

Before:
  public FolderService(...) {
    _childrenAllReFillerManager = new ChildrenAllReFillerManager(
      profileProvider, contentManagerServiceProvider, blobStorageServiceProvider, environmentProvider, logger);
  }

After:
  public FolderService(IChildrenAllReFillerManager childrenAllReFillerManager, ...) {
    _childrenAllReFillerManager = childrenAllReFillerManager;
  }

ProfileService.GetProfileEntriesAsync uses Parallel.ForEach with .GetAwaiter().GetResult() to call async BlobStorageServiceProvider methods. This blocks thread-pool threads and can cause deadlocks or thread-pool exhaustion under ASP.NET synchronization context at scale.

Before:
  Parallel.ForEach(profiles, new ParallelOptions { MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 10 }, profile => {
    profile.ThumbnailRelativePathWithSignature = _blobStorageServiceProvider
      .GenerateThumbnailRelativePathWithSignatureAsync(profile.ThumbnailId).GetAwaiter().GetResult();
  });

After:
  var tasks = profiles.Select(async p => {
    p.ThumbnailRelativePathWithSignature = await _blobStorageServiceProvider
      .GenerateThumbnailRelativePathWithSignatureAsync(p.ThumbnailId);
  });
  await Task.WhenAll(tasks);

ContentId, ProfileVersionId, TeamSiteId, VersionId, ItemId, and FullPathId are all raw strings throughout the codebase. There is no compile-time safety preventing passing a ContentId where a VersionId is expected. The 'lf' prefix file-detection logic is duplicated in both ItemService and ContentDetailService and should live in a FullPathId value object.

Before (duplicated in 2 services):
  private const string LIBRARY_CONTENT_PREFIX = "lf";
  return lastId.StartsWith(LIBRARY_CONTENT_PREFIX);

After:
  public record FullPathId(string Value) {
    public bool IsFile => Value.Split('/').Last(s => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)).StartsWith("lf");
  }

FollowerService sets response.Ok = true and response.IsFolder = true directly on domain response objects. These are API presentation concerns — the domain layer should not know about client-facing 'ok' status fields or shape discriminators. These should be set in MapperService or the controller.

Before:
  response.Ok = true;
  response.IsFolder = true;
  return response;

After: Remove from FollowerService; set in MapperService when mapping FollowerResponse → FollowerResource.
